<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:30:17 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Americas</category><title>At least five people shot in DC neighbourhood near the White House</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-at-least-five-people-shot-in-dc-neighbourhood-near-the-white-house</link><description>
At least one person died after five people were shot early Thursday in a Washington, DC neighbourhood near the White House, police said. A swarm of officers responded to a nearby apartment building where a suspect was barricaded and later shot himself.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e0e7178a-deaa-11f1-a92b-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316527860423.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e0e7178a-deaa-11f1-a92b-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316527860423.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7d350e28-dea9-11f1-b61f-799be286f464</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:01:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e0e7178a-deaa-11f1-a92b-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26316527860423.jpg">© Tom Brenner, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth reprimanded at war memorial</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-defense-secretary-pete-hegseth-reprimanded-at-war-memorial</link><description>
US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth, along with his wife and aides, was silenced by a guard on Wednesday at the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier. Hegseth's group was at Arlington National Cemetery for a Veterans Day ceremony when they were reprimanded for laughing and taking pictures in front of the sombre memorial.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4a303f6-deaf-11f1-971a-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/Title-Hegseth-vid.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4a303f6-deaf-11f1-971a-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/Title-Hegseth-vid.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">02ab887e-deb0-11f1-ba6c-4f360315101f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:51:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang resigns after revelations on extramarital affairs</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-resigns-after-revelations-on-extramarital-affairs</link><description>
Jensen Huang resigned as chief executive of AI giant Nvidia on Thursday, November 12, after revelations he had two extramarital affairs, including one with a woman accused of spying for China. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Washington Fraser Jackson and FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert have more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/81e0e920-dea8-11f1-b25e-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6e42fb5f.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/81e0e920-dea8-11f1-b25e-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6e42fb5f.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">820f523e-dea7-11f1-953a-5f087d0586d2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:46:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mississippi elects its first African American to US Senate since Reconstruction</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-mississippi-elects-its-first-african-american-to-us-senate-since-reconstruction</link><description>
Democrat Scott Colom defeated Republican Senator Cindy Hyde-Smith to become Mississippi’s first Black US Senator since Reconstruction. His narrow victory, confirmed on November 11 after prolonged ballot counting, marks a major political shift in the conservative state. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Douglas Herbert has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b06874ba-de90-11f1-bdf7-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T115424Z-858832477-RC2BMOA4L75G-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-MISSISSIPPI.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b06874ba-de90-11f1-bdf7-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T115424Z-858832477-RC2BMOA4L75G-RTRMADP-3-USA-ELECTION-MISSISSIPPI.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">529433fe-de8d-11f1-b81b-a9beaa3f8cda</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:23:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Huang powers and bankrolls AI revolution: Nvidia CEO caught between 'a rock and a very hard place'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-he-powers-and-bankrolls-ai-revolution-nvidia-ceo-huang-caught-between-rock-and-a-very-hard-place-1</link><description>
Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Bernard Benhamou, Secretary General of France's Institute of Digital Sovereignty. Benhamou examines the intersection of traditional espionage, geopolitical rivalry and the extraordinary concentration of power within the global AI industry. Discussing allegations surrounding Nvidia's leadership, he describes the chipmaker as "the banker of the global AI system," a striking characterization that captures the company's importance not merely as a semiconductor manufacturer, but as a central actor in the economic and technological infrastructure underpinning the AI boom. "Because humans stay humans." Benhamou identifies one of the central paradoxes of the artificial intelligence revolution: even as technological systems acquire unprecedented strategic and economic importance, the individuals who control them remain susceptible to familiar forms of influence, manipulation and misjudgment.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a751712-de89-11f1-bfe8-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-080447-081419-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a751712-de89-11f1-bfe8-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-080447-081419-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">704c669a-de89-11f1-bc24-433772713d41</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:11:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Paraguayans get some savings back after banking collapse disrupted economy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-paraguayans-get-some-savings-back-after-banking-collapse-disrupted-economy</link><description>
Paraguay's Central Bank said Wednesday, November 11, it had partially returned savings to all eligible Ueno Bank depositors locked out of their accounts when it collapsed last week. The digital bank's takeover on November 3 triggered massive protests across Paraguay and led to the impeachment and arrest of ex-president Santiago Pena, who is linked to Ueno.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6cc7d94-de87-11f1-b257-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-70458b4a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d6cc7d94-de87-11f1-b257-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-70458b4a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">87e20e0a-de83-11f1-a240-617a17dbda2a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:24:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Scott Colom makes history in Mississippi as first Black senator in more than 140 years</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261112-scott-colom-makes-history-in-mississippi-as-first-black-senator-in-more-than-140-years</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, November 12: We look at reactions from Spain after the country's first nationwide general strike in 14 years. It comes two weeks before snap general elections. Also: Scott Colom makes history as the first Black senator in Mississippi in 145 years after an epic Senate midterm race finally concluded. Finally, fans of Barça will be able to inter their ashes at Camp Nou as part of a new offer by the club to allow supporters to cheer on the team in the afterlife.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abaf12d8-de6a-11f1-a854-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-11-12T07-26-01-411Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/abaf12d8-de6a-11f1-a854-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-11-12T07-26-01-411Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f670b25e-de6a-11f1-935a-c305a618e15b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:50:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mississippi Democrat Scott Colom flips US Senate seat in stunning upset</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/mississippi-democrat-scott-colom-flips-us-senate-seat-in-stunning-upset</link><description>
In a historic upset, Democrat Scott Colom has won his US Senate race in traditionally conservative Mississippi, networks projected Wednesday, making him the first African American elected to the chamber from the southern state in more than 140 years. Report by Morgan Ayre
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ba06506-de6e-11f1-b456-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-083435-083629-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ba06506-de6e-11f1-b456-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-083435-083629-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">90d10274-de6e-11f1-95fd-2d2c4544fe14</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:39:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Who is Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/who-is-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang</link><description>
Nvidia's board met late Wednesday to decide whether to oust CEO ​Jensen Huang, a source familiar with the matter told Reuters, as the world's dominant supplier of AI chips grapples with fallout from reports of two extramarital affairs involving its longtime leader. Report by Jack Pownall and Eliza Herbert.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d05a8646-de6d-11f1-b785-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-083205-083407-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d05a8646-de6d-11f1-b785-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-083205-083407-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d53df7a6-de6d-11f1-b2f0-97db8bd86508</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:54:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Nvidia board weighs ouster of CEO Jensen Huang amid spy scandal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-nvidia-board-weighs-ouster-of-ceo-jensen-huang-amid-spy-scandal</link><description>
Nvidia's board met late Wednesday to consider removing chief executive Jensen Huang, after reports of two extramarital affairs, including one with an alleged Chinese spy, fuelled a market sell-off and raised questions about the AI chipmaker's leadership.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/adc9839a-de43-11f1-b3fb-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/8ddea3d92713a356312bc00778a8eceba072dea5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/adc9839a-de43-11f1-b3fb-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/8ddea3d92713a356312bc00778a8eceba072dea5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">43f3891a-de4e-11f1-8f78-31a8d87c777b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:05:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/adc9839a-de43-11f1-b3fb-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/8ddea3d92713a356312bc00778a8eceba072dea5.jpg">© I-Hwa Cheng, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Paraguay partially refunds Ueno Bank depositors after collapse</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261112-paraguay-partially-refunds-ueno-bank-depositors-after-collapse</link><description>
Paraguay's Central Bank said Wednesday it had partially returned savings to all eligible Ueno Bank depositors, following the lender's collapse last week. The crisis triggered mass protests and the impeachment and arrest of former president Santiago Peña, who is accused of directing government funds to the bank.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe9ccf8c-de3b-11f1-9318-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26313615647131.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe9ccf8c-de3b-11f1-9318-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26313615647131.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">80a359e8-de27-11f1-b809-670d3cc03bfb</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:11:52 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fe9ccf8c-de3b-11f1-9318-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26313615647131.jpg">© Jorge Saenz, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Democrat Scott Colom wins historic Senate race in Mississippi</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-democrat-scott-colom-wins-historic-senate-race-in-mississippi</link><description>
Democrat Scott Colom defeated Republican Senator Cindy Hyde-Smith in Mississippi after a final count on Wednesday, becoming the state's first Black US senator since Reconstruction. His narrow victory adds to the Democrats' midterm gains as President Donald Trump's party suffers a series of defeats.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7807fc4-de27-11f1-b242-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314768923953.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7807fc4-de27-11f1-b242-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314768923953.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3af0db02-de2a-11f1-b2bd-4955f5751d59</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:47:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e7807fc4-de27-11f1-b242-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314768923953.jpg">© Ellen Schmidt, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo XIV returns to second homeland Peru and a nationwide welcome</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-pope-leo-xiv-returns-to-second-homeland-peru-to-a-nationwide-welcome</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV arrived in Peru on Wednesday for the final leg of his South American tour, returning to the country where he spent more than two decades as a missionary and bishop. Thousands gathered to welcome him home as “Padre Robert”, with many hoping his visit will bring attention to the country's poverty, crime and political instability.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c7939ee-de21-11f1-adfe-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T224025Z-451595732-RC2YLOAKZZON-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c7939ee-de21-11f1-adfe-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T224025Z-451595732-RC2YLOAKZZON-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">afeb08d4-de29-11f1-81c1-8fedcbdbcc33</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:43:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c7939ee-de21-11f1-adfe-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-11T224025Z-451595732-RC2YLOAKZZON-RTRMADP-3-POPE-LATAM-PERU.jpg">© Yara Nardi, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Failed state: Haiti has collapsed in a kind of a black hole'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/bukele-says-salvadoran-troops-destroyed-gang-hq-in-haiti</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Jean Marie Théodat, Author and Head of the Geography Department at Paris 1 Panthéon-Sorbonne University. He describes Haiti as a failed state: "Haiti has collapsed in a kind of a black hole. I mean there is no president, no elections, no chambers of deputies, no senators." Addressing the reported deployment of Salvadoran troops to Haiti, he says “when you are dying, you don't look at the hand that brings help,” explaining why many Haitians may welcome military assistance from Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele despite concerns about his government's authoritarian methods and the uncertain political consequences of foreign intervention. Drawing on a Haitian proverb, he warns that “a goat with several masters can die of thirst while tied up,” underscoring the dangers of poorly coordinated interventions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f6655d8-dded-11f1-926e-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261111-151842-152903-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2f6655d8-dded-11f1-926e-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261111-151842-152903-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">33f1f422-dded-11f1-8600-530574a1d80e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:38:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil electoral court fines Meta $1.3 MN, sees no deliberate election bias</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-electoral-court-fines-meta-1-3-mn-sees-no-deliberate-election-bias</link><description>
Jan Onoszko, our correspondent in Rio, has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c4a5b334-dde6-11f1-9c6b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261111-161101-161439-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c4a5b334-dde6-11f1-9c6b-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261111-161101-161439-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c96c68cc-dde6-11f1-b98a-c593be1822fb</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:08:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US House votes to derail impeachment of Defense Secretary Hegseth</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-house-votes-to-derail-impeachment-of-defense-secretary-hegseth</link><description>
Republicans in ​the US House ​of Representatives banded together on Tuesday ​to ‌derail ⁠aneffort to impeach ‌Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth. Fraser Jackson, our correspondant in Washington DC, has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f9877d4-ddc9-11f1-b424-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-10T155719Z-652015653-RC23LOADBZX1-RTRMADP-3-USA-POLAND.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f9877d4-ddc9-11f1-b424-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-10T155719Z-652015653-RC23LOADBZX1-RTRMADP-3-USA-POLAND.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3da2ba66-ddc9-11f1-a0e7-d9e11bf78434</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:17:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Welcome Home': Peru awaits Pope Leo's emotional 'homecoming'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/welcome-home-peru-awaits-pope-leo-s-emotional-homecoming</link><description>
Pope Leo will wrap ​up his visit to Argentina on Wednesday during his 12-day South America tour, with a final event expected to draw millions, before traveling to Peru in an emotional homecoming for the first Peruvian citizen to lead the Catholic Church.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d11fc4ac-ddc2-11f1-966c-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261111-121133-121335-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d11fc4ac-ddc2-11f1-966c-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261111-121133-121335-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6582a54-ddc2-11f1-9b30-cd4db83ef990</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:53:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pope Leo to end Argentina tour with outdoor mass before Peru 'homecoming'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261111-pope-leo-to-end-argentina-tour-with-large-outdoor-mass-before-emotional-peru-homecoming</link><description>
Pope Leo will conclude his three-day visit to Argentina Wednesday with an outdoor mass expected to draw millions before continuing his tour of South America by travelling to Peru, where he once served as a missionary. The pontiff plans to deliver a speech in front of Peruvian President Keiko Fujimori, whose election earlier this year was marred ‌by fraud accusations and vote-counting delays.
